  "title": "Erdős Problem #990",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f=a_0+\\cdots+a_dx^d\\in \\mathbb{C}[x]$ be a polynomial. Is it true that, if $f$ has roots $z_1,\\ldots,z_d$ with corresponding arguments $\\theta_1,\\ldots,\\theta_d\\in [0,2\\pi]$, then for all intervals $I\\subseteq [0,2\\pi]$ $ \\left\\lvert (\\# \\theta_i \\in I) - \\frac{\\lvert I\\rvert}{2\\pi}d\\right\\rvert \\ll \\left(n\\log M\\right)^{1/2}, $ where $n$ is the number of non-zero coefficients of $f$ and $ M=\\frac{\\lvert a_0\\rvert+\\cdots +\\lvert a_d\\rvert}{(\\lvert a_0\\rvert\\lvert a_d\\rvert)^{1/2}}. $ ",
    "sha256": "d73eee7544dab5f08a8855445385c870caac0e1c64c5a6ea715e661e7292fabe",
